# Configuration for running this project
#
# There is currently nothing to configure. This app is frontend-only — every
# screen (student, instructor, admin) runs on mock data held in src/lib/*.ts
# and in-browser state (React state + localStorage). There is no database,
# no API keys, and no `process.env` usage anywhere in the codebase.
#
# To run the project:
#   npm install
#   npm run dev
#
# This file is kept as a placeholder for when backend work starts (database
# connection string, auth secrets, etc.) so contributors have one obvious
# place to look. Copy it to `.env` and fill in values once those variables
# actually exist in the code — don't add speculative ones here in the
# meantime, since anything listed below would be misleading until it's
# actually read by the app.
